Results:

```text
46,772  fail the zero law
   178  pass zero but fail unary n=1
    66  have a certified head-diverging zero computation
     0  unresolved
     0  survivors
```

The checker first used bounded reductions. The 66 fuel cases were then resolved by actual reductions to four explicit head-loop patterns—not classified from fuel exhaustion:

```text
D D → D D                         D = \t. t t

G G → G G c                       G = \t. t t c

G' G' → G' G' (\u. c)             G' = \t. t t (\u. c)

H (K H) → (K H) c (K H)
        → H (K H)                 H = \t. t c t
```

These remain head-divergent with arbitrary trailing operands. The respective counts were `20, 29, 6, 11`.

This is an exhaustive computational exclusion with explicit divergence arguments, **not a Lean-checked theorem**. Unlike a finite battery supporting a candidate, the zero and `n=1` failures suffice to refute every member of this finite source family.

The full run took approximately **1.1 seconds**, plus **0.14 seconds** to finish the remaining loop certificates, using one thread. A preliminary normal-argument-only pass examined 29,208 candidates; even counting both passes, fewer than 100,000 candidate visits occurred.

